course: dictionary
lesson: 15281
title: Happening at the same time
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Simultaneous is an adjective. It describes things that happen at exactly the same time. «The two fireworks gave a simultaneous bang.» Both bangs happened at one moment, not one after the other.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence, such as «at the same time», «together» or «in the same moment». «Mum and Dad gave a simultaneous shout of surprise.» They shouted in the same moment, so simultaneous fits. Check by swapping in «at the same time» and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In maths, simultaneous equations are two or more equations that must be true at the same time, and you solve them together. You do not need to solve them yet. Just know the word means "at once, together", not "one after another".
fact: Simultaneous means happening or done at exactly the same time.
fact: Simultaneous is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a simultaneous shout, a simultaneous flash.
fact: «Simultaneous equations» are two or more equations that must be true at the same time, solved together.
fact: «Simultaneous translation» means translating speech as it is being spoken.
fact: Things that happen one after another are not simultaneous.
exercise: «The two lights gave a simultaneous flash.» What does simultaneous mean here? | *Happening at exactly the same time | Very bright | Happening one after another | Coloured red and blue
exercise: «Mum and Dad gave a simultaneous shout of surprise.» Which word tells you they shouted at the same moment? | surprise | shout | Mum | *simultaneous
exercise: Sam says, «The two runners finished one after another, so their finish was simultaneous.» Is Sam right? | No, because runners never finish | Yes, because runners always finish together | Yes, one after another is simultaneous | *No, one after another is not simultaneous
test: «The two fireworks gave a simultaneous bang.» What is the best meaning of simultaneous? | Happening slowly, bit by bit | Coming from far away | Very loud and frightening | *Happening at exactly the same moment
test: In maths, what are simultaneous equations? | Equations that are solved one after another | Equations with no answer | Equations about shapes and angles | *Two or more equations that must be true at the same time
exam: Which sentence uses simultaneous correctly? | The cat was very simultaneous. | *The two lights gave a simultaneous flash. | The simultaneous was tall and green. | We simultaneous to the park after lunch.
